Swap any person into a photo while keeping the background, lighting, and detail 100% real — this ComfyUI inpainting workflow uses Z-Image Turbo, automatic SAM masking, face/eye detailer passes, and an optional Flux 2 Klein enhancement step to blend the result seamlessly. No manual masking, no mismatched lighting, no wrecked backgrounds — just clean, realistic person inpainting from start to finish.
 
In this video I break down the full ComfyUI workflow node-by-node: how the automatic person detection and masking pipeline works, how the Z-Image Turbo inpainting step regenerates only the masked subject, how the face and eye detailer passes add fine detail without redrawing the whole face, and how the optional Flux mask enhancement pass cleans up inpainting seams for a final result that holds up under close inspection. I also cover every setting worth tweaking — denoise values, detection thresholds, mask smoothing, and more — so you can adapt this workflow to your own subjects and source photos.
 
